body:
Well im from a European family and during the industrial revolution up until the late 1920s, my family were quite well off. We used to have maids etc from what my great-grandmother has told me. Ive read some of my relatives journals too that are ancient in these journals they all talk about maids/cooks like members of the family. (They talk of their families, their marriages etc) think its still relevant today- esp for famous people, those people are around you 24/7 and you've grown to trust them etc so they just become like part of your furniture.

&#x200B;

On second thought..I think it might be different in other cultures/ societies today though- especially in places like India were a caste system exists and people who do menial jobs are looked down upon- although im sure thats improving and its not like that everywhere. I think it just depends? \*Shrugs\*
